(Bug #100: the zero-width fix widens what counts as a width - a bare `0`
 or all-zeros is now a legal width of 0 - but must not widen what counts
 as a BASE specifier. Zeros followed by a letter that is none of `x`,
 `X`, `b`, `o` is still zeros then junk, and junk stays an
 unknown-specifier error exactly as #98 requires; it never falls into
 the same no-op `{n:0}` gets on its own.)

a number called n is 42.
Print "{n:0q}".
